dzn: Ika fixes for Vulkan 1.3 and enhanced barriers

- A layout transition's barrier waits for all later work (SyncAfter = ALL):
  D3D12 orders the transition only against SyncAfter, while Vulkan completes
  it before every destination stage and lets later barriers chain off them.
  3DMark Wild Life Extreme read a depth buffer in compute before its
  decompression finished and showed spreading black tiles.
- Attachments in the GENERAL layout are rendered in the render target and
  depth/stencil write layouts for the duration of the pass; the common
  layouts allow no attachment writes.
- Images with concurrent sharing use the COMMON layout instead of UNDEFINED,
  which discarded them and dropped their synchronization.
- A transition from UNDEFINED keeps the wait on its source stages.
- Application barriers never end in SYNC_NONE/NO_ACCESS, which forbids any
  later access in the same submission.
- The attachment stages also wait for render pass resolves, vertex input for
  vertex shading, draw indirect for the compute pass that rewrites arguments.
- Multisampled clears on compute queues go through a scratch render target
  cleared asynchronously and waited for on the GPU at submission; on direct
  queues the clear is recorded inline.
- Dynamic state: patch control points for a dynamic topology, FRONT_AND_BACK
  culling disables rasterization only for polygons, depth writes need the
  depth test, per-face stencil mask usage from the effective state.
- Coherent storage buffers are marked per binding instead of shader-wide.
- VK_EXT_4444_formats, VK_EXT_texel_buffer_alignment, minImageTransferGranularity
  of one, a checked map of the inline uniform buffer, descriptor heap errors
  logged with the device removed reason.
- DZN_DEBUG switches nomediump16, noenhancedbarriers, api12, nodiscard and the
  DZN_HIDE_EXTS list for testing.

